<title>SWEDEN: Sweden's Modo sees price rise succeeding.</title>
<headline>Sweden's Modo sees price rise succeeding.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish forestry group Modo said it believed its announced pulp price rise to $580 per tonne from May 1 would be successful.</p>
<p>&quot;I believe this will go through even if there may be a little delay,&quot; company chairman Bengt Pettersson told a news conference.  </p>
<p>Pettersson pointed out that major U.S. pulp producers had been successful in driving through increases. -- Simon Haydon, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1004</p>
